      "writtenOn": "2023-02-06T15:12:56Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "I can\u0027t see how this is a problem. The default cpp_std is c++17. So everything that had C++17 didn\u0027t actually change anything if this was removed from it. It only affects the targets that compiles under C++20 and if a module was compiling under C++20 then it\u0027ll still have `cpp_std`.\n\nIn summary,\n\n* If a target had `cpp_std: c++17` then removing it doesn\u0027t make any difference.\n* If a target had `cpp_std: c++20` then it shouldn\u0027t be remove as there\u0027s currently no higher C++ version supported?\n* There\u0027re no target using cpp_std less than 17.",
